@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    THE SHELL. The window is a column: the application area on top, the status frame along the
    bottom. The frame is a sibling of .page, not a child of main, so it spans the FULL window
    width - under the sidebar as well as the content - and is window chrome rather than a
    footer belonging to whatever module is open.

    It was first built inside main, which made it stop where the sidebar stops and read as part
    of the page. Owner, 2026-10-01: "why isn't it a frame across the bottom of the window? why
    is it just a footer on the module page? that is not what I told you to design."

    The height chain from queue item 22 is preserved and extended rather than bypassed:
    .app-shell owns the 100vh, .page takes what is left with `flex: 1; min-height: 0`, and the
    frame is `flex: none`. No element guesses the height of any other, which is the property
    item 22 bought. Nothing here is fixed or absolute, so nothing overlays page content - that
    was item 22's actual defect. See MainLayout.razor.css and AppLayoutCssTests.
*@
<div class="app-shell">
    <div class="page">
        <div class="sidebar">
            <NavMenu />
        </div>

        <main>
            <div class="top-row px-4 d-flex justify-content-end align-items-center">
                <AuthorizeView>
                    <Authorized>
                        <UsageTracker />
                        <ThemePicker />
                        <small class="text-muted">
                            <span class="me-1">&#128100;</span>@context.User.Identity?.Name
                        </small>
                    </Authorized>
                </AuthorizeView>
            </div>

            <article class="content px-4">
                @Body
            </article>
        </main>
    </div>

    <AuthorizeView>
        <Authorized>
            @*
                Warns before navigating away from running work and cancels it on OK. Rendered
                once here rather than per page: a per-page guard would need adding to 36 pages
                and would silently miss any that forgot - the same failure shape as the
                per-module spinners this system replaces.
            *@
            <InFlightWorkGuard />
            <GlobalProgress />
        </Authorized>
    </AuthorizeView>
</div>

<div id="blazor-error-ui">
    An unhandled error has occurred.
    <a href="" class="reload">Reload</a>
    <a class="dismiss">&#x2715;</a>
</div>
